1
00:00:01,334 --> 00:00:02,793
"Previously on The Mentalist..."

2
00:00:03,002 --> 00:00:07,965
Our fugitive is a known associate
of the serial killer Red John.

3
00:00:08,257 --> 00:00:11,385
She's wanted for murder,
conspiracy, kidnapping

4
00:00:11,552 --> 00:00:12,595
and weapons violation.

5
00:00:12,762 --> 00:00:14,514
Lorelei has taken a hostage.

6
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:15,806
Need a ride?

7
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:17,892
Lorelei hasn't contacted me
in years.

8
00:00:18,267 --> 00:00:22,939
I'm guessing you had a vain,
selfish, and controlling mother

9
00:00:23,231 --> 00:00:25,066
and you found the strength
to pull away.

10
00:00:25,358 --> 00:00:27,235
I sold Lorelei's sister.

11
00:00:27,401 --> 00:00:29,487
I don't remember reading
anything about a sister.

12
00:00:29,737 --> 00:00:32,448
Miranda.
That was her name.

13
00:00:32,740 --> 00:00:33,866
Where is Miranda now?

14
00:00:34,075 --> 00:00:37,119
She's... she was murdered.
She's dead.

15
00:00:37,286 --> 00:00:40,206
Losing my sister brought me
into my full reality.

16
00:00:40,414 --> 00:00:42,875
- Nothing can hurt me.
- It's nonsense, believe me.

17
00:00:43,459 --> 00:00:44,585
Things can hurt you.

18
00:00:44,794 --> 00:00:46,963
Jane, what's going on?
Have you been kidnapped?

19
00:00:47,088 --> 00:00:49,924
Yes. I'm in fear of my life.
I can't talk long.

20
00:00:50,049 --> 00:00:51,092
What happened to Miranda?

21
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:54,345
Before Miranda died she carved a message
into the warehouse floor.

22
00:00:54,637 --> 00:00:56,013
- What'd it say?
- It says "Roy."

23
00:00:56,556 --> 00:00:59,475
Your buddy Red John...
he killed your sister.

24
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:00,643
That's not true.

25
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:02,061
- You don't want it to be true.
- Just stop!

26
00:01:02,395 --> 00:01:03,729
God, you're just like him.

27
00:01:03,938 --> 00:01:06,148
I only wonder why the two of you
didn't become lifelong friends

28
00:01:06,274 --> 00:01:07,567
the moment you shook hands.

29
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:10,278
I'm never gonna convince you
that Red John killed your sister.

30
00:01:10,861 --> 00:01:13,072
You need to go and find out
the truth for yourself.

31
00:01:13,823 --> 00:01:15,074
You know where to find me.

32
00:01:53,154 --> 00:01:54,196
Hey.

33
00:02:14,967 --> 00:02:16,010
Wake up.

34
00:02:26,604 --> 00:02:27,813
Hello, Julia.

35
00:02:30,775 --> 00:02:32,360
What do you want?

36
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:35,029
You know exactly
what I want.

37
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:51,003
You want me to stop?

38
00:02:52,254 --> 00:02:53,839
Then tell me
what I wanna know.

39
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:58,969
I told you.

40
00:03:00,721 --> 00:03:02,139
I don't know anything.

41
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:12,733
You don't know anything, huh?

42
00:03:14,026 --> 00:03:17,738
I don't know.
I didn't know your sister...

43
00:03:21,742 --> 00:03:25,663
- Sure about that?
- I don't... I don't know anything.

44
00:03:31,752 --> 00:03:33,212
You sure you don't know?

45
00:03:36,132 --> 00:03:39,427
Okay!
I'll talk, please. Just...

46
00:03:40,761 --> 00:03:41,804
Stop!

47
00:03:49,019 --> 00:03:52,523
I wasn't involved
with your sister's death.

48
00:04:00,197 --> 00:04:03,075
This Lorelei Martins...she broke
into the home last night.

49
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:06,454
She assaulted the victim,
cuffed her hands and feet

50
00:04:07,163 --> 00:04:08,914
and tortured her
for well over an hour.

51
00:04:09,373 --> 00:04:12,334
- Does this have audio?
- Unfortunately, no.

52
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,086
We don't know
what they're discussing.

53
00:04:14,712 --> 00:04:16,172
How did you get this on tape?

54
00:04:16,547 --> 00:04:18,716
We found a nanny cam
hidden in the living room.

55
00:04:19,175 --> 00:04:20,301
A neighbor said the victim had it

56
00:04:20,426 --> 00:04:23,554
because she suspected
the housekeeper was stealing.

57
00:04:24,138 --> 00:04:26,557
Well, we appreciate Sac P.D.
bringing us the case.

58
00:04:57,544 --> 00:04:58,587
Hey, boss.

59
00:04:58,754 --> 00:05:01,548
Victim's name is Julia Howard.
38, single, lives alone.

60
00:05:01,882 --> 00:05:04,176
She manages a battered women's shelter
here in Sacramento.

61
00:05:04,802 --> 00:05:07,137
{\an8}Doesn't seem like the kind of person
Lorelei would target.

62
00:05:07,596 --> 00:05:09,848
No, she doesn't.
Family, friends, co-workers...

63
00:05:10,432 --> 00:05:11,475
{\an8}they all say Julia was a saint.

64
00:05:11,767 --> 00:05:13,769
{\an8}Dedicated her life
to helping others.

65
00:05:14,269 --> 00:05:15,896
So why did Lorelei kill her?

66
00:05:16,688 --> 00:05:17,731
{\an8}Any thoughts?

67
00:05:19,525 --> 00:05:20,567
{\an8}Jane?

68
00:05:21,401 --> 00:05:22,861
{\an8}No, no thoughts.

69
00:05:23,362 --> 00:05:26,323
{\an8}Okay, you and Rigsby need to look
into every aspect of Lorelei's life...

70
00:05:26,532 --> 00:05:28,700
{\an8}her mother, her sister Miranda
even Red John.

71
00:05:28,867 --> 00:05:31,119
We need to find the connection
between Lorelei and our victim.

72
00:05:31,245 --> 00:05:32,287
You got it.

73
00:05:36,416 --> 00:05:38,335
{\an8}- No thoughts?
- No.

74
00:05:42,798 --> 00:05:43,841
This is Lisbon.

75
00:05:45,217 --> 00:05:46,885
{\an8}Yes, sir.
I'll be right there.

76
00:05:47,803 --> 00:05:50,222
{\an8}- It's Bertram. I gotta go.
- Okay.

77
00:05:52,516 --> 00:05:53,559
{\an8}You coming?

78
00:05:55,394 --> 00:05:56,436
No. Sorry.

79
00:06:06,154 --> 00:06:08,282
- Am I interrupting?
- Oh, no, no. Come on in.

80
00:06:09,449 --> 00:06:11,785
{\an8}Teresa, you remember Bob Kirkland
from Homeland Security?

81
00:06:12,494 --> 00:06:14,162
- Of course.
- Agent Lisbon.

82
00:06:14,413 --> 00:06:17,541
{\an8}Bob and his team
were interested to hear

83
00:06:17,666 --> 00:06:18,959
{\an8}about the return
of Lorelei Martins.

84
00:06:19,167 --> 00:06:20,210
Can imagine.

85
00:06:20,419 --> 00:06:23,463
{\an8}Her arrest continues
to be a priority for Homeland.

86
00:06:23,672 --> 00:06:27,134
{\an8}I've heard you say that in the past
but you've never said why.

87
00:06:27,551 --> 00:06:30,262
Lorelei Martins is a known
associate of Red John.

88
00:06:30,429 --> 00:06:31,763
She escaped from prison.

89
00:06:31,889 --> 00:06:33,807
She kidnapped
your colleague Patrick Jane.

90
00:06:33,932 --> 00:06:36,852
{\an8}Which are all valid reasons
for the CBI to be involved

91
00:06:37,019 --> 00:06:38,061
but Homeland?

92
00:06:38,478 --> 00:06:39,855
You deal with terrorists.

93
00:06:40,063 --> 00:06:42,566
{\an8}We have a wide range
of investigative interests.

94
00:06:43,734 --> 00:06:45,694
{\an8}- I have to learn that trick.
- Which?

95
00:06:46,111 --> 00:06:48,530
How you speak
without saying anything.

96
00:06:48,655 --> 00:06:50,282
Well, I'll try to be more direct.

97
00:06:50,782 --> 00:06:52,868
{\an8}Director Bertram has been
kind enough to offer

98
00:06:52,993 --> 00:06:55,829
{\an8}CBI's resources
in finding Lorelei Martins.

99
00:06:56,288 --> 00:06:57,331
Sir?

100
00:06:57,456 --> 00:07:00,417
{\an8}Well, you and Homeland
won't be working together directly

101
00:07:00,584 --> 00:07:02,336
{\an8}but Kirkland and his team
will have full access

102
00:07:02,544 --> 00:07:03,754
to your investigation.

103
00:07:05,964 --> 00:07:07,215
We'd like to be kept
in the loop.

104
00:07:22,481 --> 00:07:25,233
Bertram is bringing Homeland in
on the Lorelei murder.

105
00:07:29,988 --> 00:07:31,031
Did you hear me?

106
00:07:33,325 --> 00:07:34,368
{\an8}Yes.

107
00:07:37,537 --> 00:07:38,789
{\an8}Now that she's killed someone

108
00:07:38,997 --> 00:07:40,749
{\an8}they're gonna start looking again
into her escape.

109
00:07:41,083 --> 00:07:42,125
That's likely.

110
00:07:42,334 --> 00:07:46,421
Jane. I know you broke her out of prison
and you know I know.

111
00:07:46,797 --> 00:07:49,383
{\an8}- And I know you know I know.
- This is not funny.

112
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:53,136
If they find out you could be charged
as an accomplice to murder.

113
00:07:53,261 --> 00:07:54,304
{\an8}Well, if they find out.

114
00:07:54,763 --> 00:07:57,224
{\an8}They won't, unless, of course,
you sing to the coppers.

115
00:07:57,432 --> 00:08:00,102
Which I won't, and that makes me
an accomplice to murder as well.

116
00:08:00,268 --> 00:08:02,479
Well, only if you look at it
like a very persnickety lawyer.

117
00:08:02,688 --> 00:08:04,189
She tortured someone.

118
00:08:04,439 --> 00:08:06,608
{\an8}Yeah. It's...it's horrible,
I-I know.

119
00:08:06,733 --> 00:08:08,235
{\an8}But she must have had
good reason.

120
00:08:08,777 --> 00:08:11,238
- God, can you hear yourself?
- Yes, I hear myself.

121
00:08:11,446 --> 00:08:14,449
{\an8}Julia Howard must have helped
murder Lorelei's sister

122
00:08:15,534 --> 00:08:16,910
must have been there
with Red John.

123
00:08:17,285 --> 00:08:19,454
Lorelei wouldn't do this
otherwise. I trust her.

124
00:08:25,335 --> 00:08:27,546
Jane... I am your partner,
not her.

125
00:08:27,754 --> 00:08:29,673
You need to be honest
with me.

126
00:08:30,173 --> 00:08:31,216
I know.

127
00:08:33,760 --> 00:08:34,928
If she contacts you

128
00:08:35,762 --> 00:08:37,806
if you find anything out
about her

129
00:08:37,931 --> 00:08:40,058
if you have any insights
into the case...

130
00:08:40,308 --> 00:08:41,351
I will tell you.

131
00:08:49,484 --> 00:08:51,820
Now the tally needs to be
filled out once every morning

132
00:08:51,945 --> 00:08:53,030
and once every evening.

133
00:08:53,196 --> 00:08:55,115
- Okay. No problem.
- Thank you, Karen.

134
00:08:56,491 --> 00:08:57,534
Hello. Can I help you?

135
00:08:57,993 --> 00:09:00,370
I guess. I'm Agent Lisbon
with the CBI.

136
00:09:00,829 --> 00:09:01,872
This is Patrick Jane.

137
00:09:01,997 --> 00:09:04,041
Kevin Rome. I'm one of the trustees
here at the shelter.

138
00:09:04,291 --> 00:09:05,917
Is there someplace
we could talk?

139
00:09:06,043 --> 00:09:08,420
We wanted to ask you some questions
about Julia Howard.

140
00:09:08,545 --> 00:09:10,297
Of course. The rest of the trustees
are right outside.

141
00:09:13,341 --> 00:09:15,343
Jane. Are you coming?

142
00:09:16,011 --> 00:09:18,096
Uh, no, I thought I'd just
take a look around

143
00:09:18,221 --> 00:09:19,514
if... that's all right.

144
00:09:19,973 --> 00:09:21,725
- Of course.
- Thank you.

145
00:09:26,438 --> 00:09:31,485
Julia was a wonderful woman
so giving, so selfless.

146
00:09:31,985 --> 00:09:33,028
I can't think of anyone

147
00:09:33,153 --> 00:09:34,362
who had a negative thing
to say about her.

148
00:09:35,530 --> 00:09:37,115
How long did Julia work
at the shelter?

149
00:09:37,616 --> 00:09:39,284
Eight years, but...

150
00:09:40,035 --> 00:09:41,411
I mean, she did
so much more than that.

151
00:09:41,536 --> 00:09:43,914
She practically ran the place
single-handedly.

152
00:09:44,039 --> 00:09:45,290
That's why we're all here...

153
00:09:45,415 --> 00:09:47,876
to try and fill in as best we
can until we find a replacement.

154
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:50,545
None of you actually worked
at the shelter.

155
00:09:51,171 --> 00:09:54,132
No, we serve an advisory role
and help with fund-raising.

156
00:09:54,508 --> 00:09:55,801
But we volunteer
when we can.

157
00:09:56,384 --> 00:09:58,929
Did you ever hear Julia
mention the name Lorelei Martins?

158
00:09:59,554 --> 00:10:02,015
- No.
- No. Is she a suspect?

159
00:10:02,474 --> 00:10:04,476
We're working
several different angles.

160
00:10:25,288 --> 00:10:28,500
I saw on the web site
that there was a fourth trustee?

161
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,628
Steven Doppler.
He's flying up from L.A. tomorrow.

162
00:10:32,003 --> 00:10:34,381
We're, uh, meeting with candidates
to fill Julia's position.

163
00:10:34,798 --> 00:10:35,841
So soon?

164
00:10:36,299 --> 00:10:38,552
The meeting was already scheduled.
It's our monthly meeting.

165
00:10:38,885 --> 00:10:41,680
I know it seems cold,
replacing her so quickly

166
00:10:41,847 --> 00:10:44,516
but the women at the shelter here
they...they've suffered enough.

167
00:10:45,142 --> 00:10:47,060
Their safety and security...
that comes first.

168
00:10:47,352 --> 00:10:48,687
Julia would have wanted that.

169
00:12:03,094 --> 00:12:04,721
How can we get in touch
with Doppler?

170
00:12:05,013 --> 00:12:07,891
He'll be with us all day tomorrow
at the Fairchild Hotel.

171
00:12:08,099 --> 00:12:09,935
That's where we're meeting
to interview new candidates.

172
00:12:10,268 --> 00:12:13,271
- Did Julia live in Sacramento?
- Jane, I'm in the middle of questioning.

173
00:12:13,396 --> 00:12:15,106
Yeah, it won't take long.
Did she?

174
00:12:15,941 --> 00:12:17,692
- Yes.
- And you're certain?

175
00:12:17,984 --> 00:12:19,027
Yes.

176
00:12:19,319 --> 00:12:21,196
She lived here for...

177
00:12:21,947 --> 00:12:25,116
For as long as I've known her.
Eight years, at least.

178
00:12:26,743 --> 00:12:28,870
- You sure?
- Pretty sure.

179
00:12:32,165 --> 00:12:33,291
Lisbon, I'm gonna head on.

180
00:12:37,629 --> 00:12:41,132
Your colleague...
he's, uh, very... odd.

181
00:12:42,050 --> 00:12:44,010
Yes. Yeah.

182
00:14:30,450 --> 00:14:31,493
Lorelei.

183
00:14:36,623 --> 00:14:37,707
Did you miss me?

184
00:14:44,629 --> 00:14:46,089
You murdered someone.

185
00:14:46,464 --> 00:14:49,175
What'd you think I was gonna do
when you set me free, Patrick?

186
00:14:49,425 --> 00:14:51,969
- You tortured them.
- I knew you'd be upset.

187
00:14:53,513 --> 00:14:55,848
You're not as tough-minded
as you'd like to think you are.

188
00:14:58,726 --> 00:15:00,269
So I wanted to see you.

189
00:15:01,062 --> 00:15:03,147
I haven't gone off the rails,
I promise.

190
00:15:03,940 --> 00:15:05,608
I know what I'm doing.

191
00:15:07,652 --> 00:15:10,571
Julia Howard got exactly
what she deserved.

192
00:15:12,156 --> 00:15:14,200
- She helped kill my sister.
- Helped who?

193
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:16,536
Not Red John.
She didn't know him.

194
00:15:17,161 --> 00:15:18,454
But I know who to go to next.

195
00:15:18,579 --> 00:15:20,623
Well, whoever that is,
they work with Red John.

196
00:15:21,207 --> 00:15:23,042
Maybe. Maybe not.

197
00:15:24,377 --> 00:15:26,504
- I'm gonna find out.
- Someone from the shelter?

198
00:15:28,214 --> 00:15:29,715
I have to go, Patrick.

199
00:15:31,300 --> 00:15:34,554
You're foolish doing this on your own.
Let me help you.

200
00:15:34,846 --> 00:15:35,888
No.

201
00:15:37,306 --> 00:15:38,808
I've done terrible things.

202
00:15:40,351 --> 00:15:42,728
Unforgivable things.
There's no way back.

203
00:15:44,730 --> 00:15:46,607
You and me are
on different roads, I hope.

204
00:15:52,613 --> 00:15:53,656
Wish me luck.

205
00:16:07,044 --> 00:16:08,588
Been doing some background
on Julia Howard

206
00:16:08,713 --> 00:16:10,006
and I think
I found something.

207
00:16:10,381 --> 00:16:11,424
She owned a home
here in Sacramento

208
00:16:11,674 --> 00:16:12,717
bought it eight years ago

209
00:16:12,842 --> 00:16:15,720
but she also leased a house in Davis
at 1309 Orchid Lane.

210
00:16:16,053 --> 00:16:18,181
I don't understand.
Was she renting it for somebody else?

211
00:16:18,306 --> 00:16:20,266
Unlikely. She doesn't have
any family in California.

212
00:16:20,516 --> 00:16:21,809
Did she even have the money
for a second house?

213
00:16:22,018 --> 00:16:23,102
Not on her salary.

214
00:16:28,774 --> 00:16:29,817
Where's Jane?

215
00:16:30,359 --> 00:16:31,652
- Haven't seen him.
- Well, thanks.

216
00:16:31,777 --> 00:16:32,820
Okay.

217
00:16:54,926 --> 00:16:55,968
Evening.

218
00:17:02,725 --> 00:17:04,936
We had an agreement.
No more lies.

219
00:17:05,353 --> 00:17:06,521
And I haven't.

220
00:17:07,230 --> 00:17:09,106
You didn't tell me
you were coming here.

221
00:17:10,399 --> 00:17:12,151
- Was Lorelei here?
- Yes.

222
00:17:12,944 --> 00:17:13,986
Damn it, Jane.

223
00:17:14,111 --> 00:17:15,863
Well, I didn't know she would be.
I was just following a lead.

224
00:17:16,280 --> 00:17:17,782
Which you didn't tell me about.

225
00:17:17,907 --> 00:17:20,326
You know, I tell you about 30%
of what I do.

226
00:17:20,535 --> 00:17:21,577
That doesn't mean
that I'm lying.

227
00:17:22,411 --> 00:17:24,664
Anyway, Lorelei confirmed
that I was right.

228
00:17:25,831 --> 00:17:27,416
Julia was involved
in Miranda's death.

229
00:17:27,667 --> 00:17:29,752
Oh, you'll have to forgive me
if I don't believe her.

230
00:17:30,169 --> 00:17:31,921
Miranda must have stayed
at Julia's shelter.

231
00:17:32,088 --> 00:17:33,464
I'll check it out.

232
00:17:33,714 --> 00:17:36,592
- Where's Lorelei now?
- She's gone. She left.

233
00:17:37,218 --> 00:17:40,054
What do you mean, she left?
Did you try and stop her?

234
00:17:40,221 --> 00:17:41,389
Well, even if I could,
I wouldn't.

235
00:17:41,556 --> 00:17:43,849
She's trying to figure out
if Red John killed her sister.

236
00:17:44,267 --> 00:17:45,518
I need to let her do that.

237
00:17:45,851 --> 00:17:49,230
And you think when Lorelei finds out
she's gonna tell you his name?

238
00:17:49,522 --> 00:17:50,565
That's the hope.

239
00:17:50,773 --> 00:17:53,568
You're putting your trust
in the mistress of a serial killer.

240
00:17:54,110 --> 00:17:56,529
- She's playing you.
- Playing me? How?

241
00:17:57,071 --> 00:17:58,364
You're blind.
You're involved with her.

242
00:17:58,489 --> 00:18:00,491
- It's clouding your judgment.
- There's no involvement.

243
00:18:01,033 --> 00:18:04,120
- I feel nothing for her.
- Now you're really lying.

244
00:18:13,087 --> 00:18:15,172
I'm gonna make this
very simple.

245
00:18:15,673 --> 00:18:17,300
I will not be a part
of this anymore

246
00:18:17,466 --> 00:18:19,719
and neither will you, if you
wanna remain with the team.

247
00:18:20,219 --> 00:18:21,262
An ultimatum?

248
00:18:22,763 --> 00:18:25,016
Someone's playing
a little too much poker.

249
00:18:31,772 --> 00:18:36,193
I confess.
I may have some feelings

250
00:18:36,319 --> 00:18:38,571
but if I have crossed
any lines

251
00:18:38,988 --> 00:18:40,656
it is not because
I like her.

252
00:18:41,198 --> 00:18:43,701
I will do anything I can
to get to Red John

253
00:18:43,826 --> 00:18:45,620
but you have known that
since the start.

254
00:18:54,712 --> 00:18:55,755
Director Bertram.

255
00:18:59,925 --> 00:19:01,302
I will be there
in the morning, sir.

256
00:19:02,637 --> 00:19:04,388
- Does he want an update?
- Yes.

257
00:19:05,973 --> 00:19:08,142
- And what are you gonna tell him?
- I don't know.

258
00:19:09,894 --> 00:19:13,773
You do realize that if Bertram and Kirkland
get to Lorelei before us, then...

259
00:19:16,150 --> 00:19:17,193
I'll never see her again.

260
00:19:19,403 --> 00:19:21,530
She won't tell me
who Red John is.

261
00:19:22,281 --> 00:19:23,616
I don't know what
to tell you, Jane.

262
00:19:32,541 --> 00:19:34,502
"No, that's fine.
No, whatever you think."

263
00:19:35,544 --> 00:19:36,796
No, no. I'm sorry.
That's fine.

264
00:19:37,004 --> 00:19:38,547
Thank you.
No, thank you, ma'am.

265
00:19:39,757 --> 00:19:40,800
All right.

266
00:19:46,347 --> 00:19:47,390
Well, where are we?

267
00:19:47,807 --> 00:19:49,600
Uh, we've made some progress.

268
00:19:51,977 --> 00:19:54,355
Unfortunately,
there's nothing substantial.

269
00:19:54,855 --> 00:19:56,982
Now I don't wanna bore you
with the details.

270
00:19:57,316 --> 00:20:01,028
I see. What about Jane?
Does he have any insights?

271
00:20:01,529 --> 00:20:04,448
You know Jane.
He's got theories.

272
00:20:04,615 --> 00:20:06,033
I love a good theory.

273
00:20:06,492 --> 00:20:09,912
If any of them were good,
I'd share 'em with you.

274
00:20:11,080 --> 00:20:12,873
You know, Lisbon,
I've always respected you

275
00:20:13,416 --> 00:20:16,669
which is why I'm going to be
completely forthcoming.

276
00:20:17,378 --> 00:20:18,421
Please.

277
00:20:19,004 --> 00:20:21,507
When it comes to Lorelei Martins
I don't think Jane can be trusted.

278
00:20:21,799 --> 00:20:22,925
I don't know if that's true.

279
00:20:23,050 --> 00:20:25,386
Well, he's admitted
to his sexual relationship with her.

280
00:20:26,303 --> 00:20:29,890
Then Martins kidnaps him
and they spend days alone together.

281
00:20:30,015 --> 00:20:32,101
And don't you ever wonder
what went on between them?

282
00:20:36,897 --> 00:20:40,025
If there's something going on,
you... you can talk to me.

283
00:20:40,943 --> 00:20:41,986
Thank you.

284
00:20:43,237 --> 00:20:44,655
I'll keep that in mind.

285
00:20:47,116 --> 00:20:48,200
If that's all...

286
00:20:50,911 --> 00:20:51,954
Great.

287
00:21:01,839 --> 00:21:02,882
What do you think?

288
00:21:10,014 --> 00:21:11,974
You work with her.
You'd know better.

289
00:21:13,642 --> 00:21:15,978
Clearly she knows more
than she's saying.

290
00:21:18,522 --> 00:21:21,150
But... good detectives
always keep their cards close.

291
00:21:23,402 --> 00:21:24,862
But can we trust her?

292
00:21:29,116 --> 00:21:30,451
Can we trust anyone?

293
00:21:34,330 --> 00:21:35,372
Morning, boss.

294
00:21:35,581 --> 00:21:37,708
Whatever you're doing, stop.
We have a lead.

295
00:21:38,083 --> 00:21:40,711
Julia Howard may have been involved
in Miranda Roman's death.

296
00:21:40,920 --> 00:21:41,962
What do we have to go on?

297
00:21:42,087 --> 00:21:43,631
It looks like Miranda
stayed at Julia's shelter.

298
00:21:43,839 --> 00:21:45,174
Find out what was
going on there.

299
00:21:45,466 --> 00:21:46,801
Sure, boss. Yeah.

300
00:22:02,191 --> 00:22:03,234
What?

301
00:22:03,359 --> 00:22:05,402
Thanks for not telling Bertram.

302
00:22:05,945 --> 00:22:07,238
I don't wanna be thanked.

303
00:22:08,489 --> 00:22:09,532
Too late.

304
00:22:46,402 --> 00:22:49,321
Hey, boss. Just got back
from the women's shelter.

305
00:22:49,488 --> 00:22:50,531
- What'd you find?
- Nothing.

306
00:22:51,115 --> 00:22:52,366
This is their official intake log.

307
00:22:53,117 --> 00:22:54,702
No evidence of Miranda Roman
ever staying there.

308
00:22:54,994 --> 00:22:56,745
- Well, that's strange.
- Here's what's stranger.

309
00:22:57,037 --> 00:22:58,497
The detective who
investigated Miranda's murder

310
00:22:58,664 --> 00:23:00,249
is positive that Miranda
stayed at the shelter.

311
00:23:00,499 --> 00:23:01,709
She had an abusive ex-boyfriend

312
00:23:01,834 --> 00:23:03,002
and spent some time there
five years ago.

313
00:23:03,294 --> 00:23:04,837
He said it would have been
a week before her death.

314
00:23:05,004 --> 00:23:06,672
All right, talk to everybody
who was on staff

315
00:23:06,881 --> 00:23:08,883
around that time and dig deeper
into their records.

316
00:23:09,300 --> 00:23:11,176
- Figure out what we're missing.
- I'm on it.

317
00:23:35,034 --> 00:23:36,410
Wait. Stop it.

318
00:23:37,828 --> 00:23:39,663
- Get off your brother.
- He's gone rogue, mom.

319
00:23:39,914 --> 00:23:40,956
Hey! Stop!

320
00:23:41,081 --> 00:23:42,124
Come on!

321
00:23:43,876 --> 00:23:44,919
She's got a gun!

322
00:23:45,753 --> 00:23:48,380
Look! She has a gun!
Run!

323
00:23:49,548 --> 00:23:50,591
Hey!

324
00:23:54,470 --> 00:23:57,222
Hey, hey!
Stop or I'll shoot!

325
00:23:58,057 --> 00:23:59,141
Get down on your knees!

326
00:24:04,939 --> 00:24:05,981
Get rid of the gun!

327
00:24:56,989 --> 00:24:58,115
- CBI?
- What happened?

328
00:24:58,407 --> 00:25:00,409
We got report of a gunman
that matches the description

329
00:25:00,617 --> 00:25:02,369
of your homicide suspect,
Lorelei Martins.

330
00:25:02,494 --> 00:25:04,329
- Was anyone killed?
- No. Security guard was injured

331
00:25:04,496 --> 00:25:05,789
but it looks like
he's gonna be okay.

332
00:25:06,206 --> 00:25:07,249
Where is she now?

333
00:25:07,499 --> 00:25:10,043
Not clear. She escaped on foot.
My men are searching the area.

334
00:25:10,669 --> 00:25:12,504
But we did find something
in the suspect's vehicle...

335
00:25:12,671 --> 00:25:15,507
a pair of handcuffs,
pliers, and a stun gun.

336
00:25:16,133 --> 00:25:17,801
She's planning
to abduct someone.

337
00:25:23,390 --> 00:25:26,601
"We were standing outside a hotel
when we heard someone screaming."

338
00:25:27,853 --> 00:25:29,563
And that's when I saw her
standing there.

339
00:25:30,814 --> 00:25:33,066
She had a gun.
She could have killed me.

340
00:25:33,483 --> 00:25:35,569
We don't believe that was
her intention.

341
00:25:36,361 --> 00:25:37,696
You don't believe?

342
00:25:38,697 --> 00:25:39,823
That's reassuring.

343
00:25:41,992 --> 00:25:43,243
Can you tell me
what she did want?

344
00:25:44,077 --> 00:25:45,787
It appears she was planning
to abduct one of you.

345
00:25:46,246 --> 00:25:47,914
Good lord. Why?

346
00:25:48,623 --> 00:25:49,666
Why the trustees?

347
00:25:50,292 --> 00:25:51,710
You think she thinks one of them
killed her sister?

348
00:25:53,045 --> 00:25:54,296
Well, it looks that way.

349
00:25:54,880 --> 00:25:57,007
Probably thinks they were helped
by Julia Howard.

350
00:25:57,883 --> 00:25:59,926
She's kinda doing
our job for us in a way.

351
00:26:00,552 --> 00:26:01,970
Shame we can't give her a call.

352
00:26:02,429 --> 00:26:03,889
Yes, it is.

353
00:26:05,390 --> 00:26:06,475
Any ideas which trustee?

354
00:26:07,851 --> 00:26:08,894
Nope.

355
00:26:13,398 --> 00:26:14,816
Did you know a woman
named Miranda Roman?

356
00:26:15,025 --> 00:26:16,401
No. Why?

357
00:26:16,902 --> 00:26:18,111
We believe she stayed
at the shelter.

358
00:26:18,320 --> 00:26:19,905
I wouldn't know
about that.

359
00:26:20,072 --> 00:26:22,282
I don't have anything to do
with the day-to-day operations.

360
00:26:22,532 --> 00:26:23,658
Who did other than Julia?

361
00:26:24,618 --> 00:26:26,620
I'm not exactly sure
what you're looking for.

362
00:26:26,828 --> 00:26:29,414
Basically, anything we can use
to determine whether or not

363
00:26:29,539 --> 00:26:31,416
someone stayed
at the shelter.

364
00:26:31,708 --> 00:26:33,335
Well, you have the official
intake log, right?

365
00:26:33,627 --> 00:26:34,669
Right.

366
00:26:34,795 --> 00:26:36,379
Other than the daily tally,
that's all there is.

367
00:26:37,089 --> 00:26:39,424
Wait. What daily tally?

368
00:26:39,549 --> 00:26:44,179
I don't know. I told you...
I was involved in fund-raising...

369
00:26:44,846 --> 00:26:46,807
parties, galas,
that sort of thing.

370
00:26:46,973 --> 00:26:50,560
At the hotel, which of the trustees
did the gunman seem to target?

371
00:26:51,311 --> 00:26:52,437
I couldn't tell you.

372
00:26:52,687 --> 00:26:55,023
Pick someone.
First name that comes to mind.

373
00:26:56,108 --> 00:26:57,150
I don't know.

374
00:26:57,275 --> 00:26:58,318
I don't know.

375
00:26:58,485 --> 00:26:59,528
I don't know.

376
00:27:01,947 --> 00:27:03,532
Hey, we got something.

377
00:27:03,865 --> 00:27:05,909
So I looked into the shelter,
and I found something strange.

378
00:27:06,326 --> 00:27:07,619
This is the shelter's official record.

379
00:27:07,953 --> 00:27:08,995
Miranda's name's missing.

380
00:27:09,121 --> 00:27:10,914
- Oh, that much we already know.
- Right.

381
00:27:11,206 --> 00:27:13,625
But the shelter also keeps
a daily tally for state records.

382
00:27:13,875 --> 00:27:15,001
It doesn't list names,
but it keeps track

383
00:27:15,127 --> 00:27:16,628
of the number of women
staying at the shelter.

384
00:27:16,962 --> 00:27:18,004
Here's what's weird.

385
00:27:18,130 --> 00:27:21,341
During Miranda's stay there's a
discrepancy between the two records.

386
00:27:21,550 --> 00:27:23,301
In the tally, there's a woman
unaccounted for.

387
00:27:23,510 --> 00:27:24,553
What does that mean?

388
00:27:24,678 --> 00:27:26,555
Well, it means someone
was doctoring the books.

389
00:27:26,721 --> 00:27:28,849
Yeah. Someone was trying to erase evidence
of Miranda Roman's stay.

390
00:27:29,015 --> 00:27:31,893
Not someone. Julia Howard.
And there's more.

391
00:27:32,060 --> 00:27:33,311
Yeah. This isn't the first time
it happened.

392
00:27:33,687 --> 00:27:36,398
So far, I've found five instances
of women unaccounted for.

393
00:27:36,648 --> 00:27:38,692
It's a pattern.
It's what it's all about.

394
00:27:39,025 --> 00:27:41,486
Okay, here's what we're gonna do.
I'm gonna release the trustees

395
00:27:41,695 --> 00:27:43,822
but I'll have an agent
sit on each of their homes.

396
00:27:43,989 --> 00:27:46,992
"Rigsby, you take Jason Lennon.
Cho, you take Kevin Rome."

397
00:27:47,200 --> 00:27:49,452
"I'll have Karl sit
on Stephen Doppler's hotel."

398
00:27:49,870 --> 00:27:50,996
"I'll take Melissa Enfield."

399
00:27:51,204 --> 00:27:53,206
"We'll be in radio contact
the entire time."

400
00:27:53,498 --> 00:27:55,333
- If Lorelei tries to go after one of them...
- She will.

401
00:27:55,834 --> 00:27:57,335
Then we'll be there to stop her.

402
00:27:59,546 --> 00:28:00,589
You're not coming.

403
00:28:01,631 --> 00:28:03,091
Yes, I am.

404
00:28:03,383 --> 00:28:05,135
Jane, listen, I know
you wanna be a part of this

405
00:28:05,260 --> 00:28:06,303
but I need you to stay...

406
00:28:06,428 --> 00:28:07,470
Well, there's no reason
for me to stay here.

407
00:28:07,637 --> 00:28:08,680
There is a reason.

408
00:28:08,847 --> 00:28:11,349
If things go wrong,
you need to be far away.

409
00:28:11,516 --> 00:28:12,601
You're in too deep.

410
00:28:15,353 --> 00:28:18,273
Jane, I'm asking you,
please stay here.

411
00:29:32,180 --> 00:29:33,431
Hey, Cho. You there?

412
00:29:34,808 --> 00:29:35,850
Yeah. What's up?

413
00:29:37,143 --> 00:29:38,395
What's going on?

414
00:29:40,105 --> 00:29:41,147
Did you need something?

415
00:29:41,564 --> 00:29:42,983
Yeah. Uh, well...

416
00:29:43,483 --> 00:29:46,403
Hey, what do you think
Van Pelt's up to right now?

417
00:29:46,861 --> 00:29:48,530
It's 5:00 a.m. She's sleeping.

418
00:29:50,615 --> 00:29:52,242
You know what I mean.

419
00:29:52,492 --> 00:29:53,576
Well, she's at a computer
training program.

420
00:29:53,785 --> 00:29:55,495
She's probably using computers.

421
00:29:56,496 --> 00:29:57,539
I should have signed up for that.

422
00:29:59,082 --> 00:30:00,834
You barely know how to turn
a computer on.

423
00:30:01,459 --> 00:30:03,628
What do you think
they teach you there? Duh.

424
00:30:36,202 --> 00:30:37,245
Hey, Jane, what's up?

425
00:30:37,370 --> 00:30:40,665
Rigsby, listen to me.
Lorelei is going after Lennon.

426
00:30:41,041 --> 00:30:42,083
Are you sure?

427
00:30:42,208 --> 00:30:44,002
Yes, I'm sure.
It's the fishing line.

428
00:30:44,336 --> 00:30:46,087
- The what?
- "Well, I'll explain later."

429
00:30:51,718 --> 00:30:53,887
Rigsby? Are you there?

430
00:31:16,326 --> 00:31:18,703
You there? Rigsby?

431
00:31:26,628 --> 00:31:28,088
"Rigsby."

432
00:31:38,556 --> 00:31:39,599
Hey, Jane.

433
00:31:39,724 --> 00:31:41,893
Lorelei is at
Jason Lennon's house.

434
00:31:42,143 --> 00:31:44,270
I think Rigsby's hurt.
We need to hurry.

435
00:31:44,979 --> 00:31:46,022
I'm on my way.

436
00:31:48,066 --> 00:31:51,694
Cho, Karl, get to Rigsby's location now.
I'm calling for backup.

437
00:32:31,609 --> 00:32:36,406
Please. Please. Don't hurt me.

438
00:32:37,073 --> 00:32:38,408
I don't wanna hurt you.

439
00:32:43,705 --> 00:32:44,747
I just wanna talk.

440
00:33:05,558 --> 00:33:07,185
Rigsby? Rigsby?

441
00:33:08,561 --> 00:33:10,396
You all right?
You're okay.

442
00:33:21,741 --> 00:33:23,701
I don't know.

443
00:33:28,998 --> 00:33:30,791
- Patrick.
- Thank God.

444
00:33:37,465 --> 00:33:39,592
I told you, I need to do this
on my own.

445
00:33:40,051 --> 00:33:41,552
No, you need my help now.

446
00:33:42,136 --> 00:33:43,596
Police will be here very soon.

447
00:33:44,889 --> 00:33:45,932
Do they know I'm here?

448
00:33:46,557 --> 00:33:48,392
No, not yet, but they soon will.

449
00:33:51,020 --> 00:33:52,313
What the hell is going on?

450
00:33:58,819 --> 00:34:00,571
Lorelei thinks this is just
about her sister

451
00:34:00,738 --> 00:34:02,615
but we both know better,
don't we?

452
00:34:03,741 --> 00:34:05,201
What are you talking about?

453
00:34:08,579 --> 00:34:10,831
You remember those other
five women from the shelter?

454
00:34:12,124 --> 00:34:14,001
The ones Julia
helped you with?

455
00:34:16,003 --> 00:34:18,714
Julia. Your partner.

456
00:34:20,216 --> 00:34:21,842
She found the most vulnerable women

457
00:34:21,968 --> 00:34:24,387
and she brought them
to you at her house.

458
00:34:24,554 --> 00:34:26,806
This is crazy!
I'm a good person!

459
00:34:27,473 --> 00:34:29,934
Okay.
So you didn't rape 'em?

460
00:34:30,476 --> 00:34:31,519
No!

461
00:34:31,894 --> 00:34:32,937
You didn't murder 'em?

462
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:39,819
You didn't bind their hands
and feet with fishing line?

463
00:34:40,444 --> 00:34:41,487
No.

464
00:34:44,532 --> 00:34:46,742
So I guess this isn't
familiar to you.

465
00:34:49,328 --> 00:34:50,371
No.

466
00:34:54,333 --> 00:34:57,169
Jason, look at me.
Look at me.

467
00:34:58,212 --> 00:34:59,463
I'm the law.

468
00:35:01,090 --> 00:35:03,384
I have to take you in.
I can't hurt you.

469
00:35:03,509 --> 00:35:04,635
I can't kill you.

470
00:35:07,221 --> 00:35:08,264
But she can.

471
00:35:10,266 --> 00:35:12,018
And if you don't tell me
the truth right now

472
00:35:12,143 --> 00:35:13,311
I'm gonna get up
and walk out of here

473
00:35:13,519 --> 00:35:14,562
and leave you two alone.

474
00:35:14,770 --> 00:35:16,480
No. Please.

475
00:35:16,897 --> 00:35:19,191
All right, now you see
it's useless lying to me.

476
00:35:19,358 --> 00:35:20,651
Tell me the truth.

477
00:35:35,708 --> 00:35:40,421
I... work... for...
Red John.

478
00:35:43,674 --> 00:35:44,717
Yeah.

479
00:35:45,676 --> 00:35:47,637
He wanted Miranda
for some reason.

480
00:35:48,012 --> 00:35:49,555
I don't know why.

481
00:35:50,973 --> 00:35:54,101
He knew her boyfriend
was abusing her.

482
00:35:56,062 --> 00:35:57,647
And she was vulnerable.

483
00:35:58,147 --> 00:35:59,398
He told me...

484
00:36:00,608 --> 00:36:02,735
to send Julia
to counsel her

485
00:36:03,152 --> 00:36:05,655
to persuade her
to come to the shelter.

486
00:36:06,739 --> 00:36:13,120
Julia brought Miranda to me
and I brought her to Red John.

487
00:36:18,584 --> 00:36:20,127
And what did Red John
do to her?

488
00:36:22,463 --> 00:36:25,257
- You know what he did.
- She needs to hear it.

489
00:36:31,305 --> 00:36:32,932
Red John...

490
00:36:33,265 --> 00:36:35,476
killed Miranda.

491
00:36:39,397 --> 00:36:40,439
I'm sorry.

492
00:36:48,114 --> 00:36:49,156
Thank you, Patrick.

493
00:37:07,675 --> 00:37:08,718
Tell me.

494
00:37:09,176 --> 00:37:10,219
Tell you what?

495
00:37:11,387 --> 00:37:12,513
Red John's name.

496
00:37:12,972 --> 00:37:15,850
Ask him.
I need a head start. Sorry.

497
00:37:16,058 --> 00:37:18,769
- Wait. We had an agreement.
- He'll talk. He's weak.

498
00:37:19,103 --> 00:37:20,396
We had an agreement.

499
00:37:20,604 --> 00:37:21,897
Well, I'm breaking it.

500
00:37:22,648 --> 00:37:24,108
I've done far worse.

501
00:37:24,900 --> 00:37:26,569
You're just gonna go kill
Red John?

502
00:37:26,986 --> 00:37:28,988
You don't think he knows
what you've been doing?

503
00:37:29,405 --> 00:37:31,365
He's got weaknesses.
He can die.

504
00:37:31,699 --> 00:37:33,075
And I'm going to kill him.

505
00:37:33,951 --> 00:37:35,327
It was good knowing you.

506
00:37:53,804 --> 00:37:54,847
Sorry.

507
00:38:08,944 --> 00:38:10,571
- You all right?
- Not really.

508
00:38:13,491 --> 00:38:14,784
- Is he okay?
- Yeah, he'll be fine.

509
00:38:14,909 --> 00:38:16,786
An ambulance is on its way.
You stay with him.

510
00:38:16,911 --> 00:38:17,953
Okay.

511
00:38:25,628 --> 00:38:28,130
Jane. What happened?

512
00:38:28,756 --> 00:38:30,007
Lorelei shot him.

513
00:38:30,382 --> 00:38:31,801
He had a pulse,
but it's gone.

514
00:38:32,551 --> 00:38:33,928
- Where is she?
- I don't know.

515
00:38:34,386 --> 00:38:35,638
Jane, let me take over.

516
00:38:35,805 --> 00:38:38,432
No, no, I got it. I got it.
He knows who Red John is.

517
00:38:44,647 --> 00:38:45,689
Come on.

518
00:38:49,151 --> 00:38:50,194
Come on.

519
00:38:53,656 --> 00:38:55,199
He had a pulse,
but I can't...

520
00:38:55,324 --> 00:38:56,492
I can't find it anymore.

521
00:39:09,755 --> 00:39:10,798
Rigsby's on the way
to the hospital.

522
00:39:10,923 --> 00:39:12,091
Good. We need to find Lorelei.

523
00:39:12,216 --> 00:39:13,717
Let's have C.H.P.
set up roadblocks.

524
00:39:13,884 --> 00:39:15,135
- She can't be far from here.
- You got it.

525
00:39:15,761 --> 00:39:16,804
What are you doing here?

526
00:39:17,888 --> 00:39:19,849
This crime scene is now
under the jurisdiction

527
00:39:20,057 --> 00:39:22,434
of Homeland Security.
Have your agents stand down.

528
00:39:23,602 --> 00:39:25,354
- Get him outta there.
- Jane, stop.

529
00:39:26,647 --> 00:39:27,690
You get away from me.

530
00:39:27,815 --> 00:39:30,442
- Step away from me.
- No. Stop. Stop it!

531
00:39:31,026 --> 00:39:32,862
- Get out of the ambulance.
- No!

532
00:39:32,987 --> 00:39:34,947
- Jason Lennon is now my witness.
- No!

533
00:39:35,114 --> 00:39:37,074
- Jane, let it go.
- No!

534
00:39:37,700 --> 00:39:38,742
Jane!

535
00:39:45,291 --> 00:39:46,375
Come on.

536
00:40:14,653 --> 00:40:15,696
Any word on Lennon?

537
00:40:16,030 --> 00:40:17,615
The doctors are keeping him
in a coma.

538
00:40:17,823 --> 00:40:19,325
They can't risk
taking him out yet.

539
00:40:19,575 --> 00:40:20,784
You can't get
the case back.

540
00:40:21,076 --> 00:40:22,745
It's only been two weeks.
I'm trying.

541
00:40:26,832 --> 00:40:28,334
Isn't why you're here, is it?

542
00:40:32,963 --> 00:40:34,298
Okay. Let's go.

543
00:41:45,828 --> 00:41:46,870
I'm sorry.

544
00:41:53,085 --> 00:41:54,128
She had it coming.

